{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration"],"title":"Events","generated":true,"anchor":"Events"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/schema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/type"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"],"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/events\/discoveredevent"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Events\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscoveredEvent"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" lists every one the program links, from every module, so a store or a tracking plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be built from it with no list to keep: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each use it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","DiscoveredEvent.all.map { $0.type.name }","\/\/ [\"ApplicationBackgrounded\", ..., \"SessionStarted\", \"signed_up\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is discovered, wherever it is declared, unless it is generic or nested in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a generic type, as neither can hold the record ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" places in the binary; the macro notes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each one where it is declared. One declared in an extension of a generic type doesn’t compile.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The library’s own events are discovered too: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Application","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" events of ","type":"text"},{"code":"LifecycleTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their modules are linked. An event that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by hand, without ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", isn’t:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list it beside the discovered ones, ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscoveredEvent.all.map(\\.type) + [Legacy.self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Limits","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An object file in a static archive that nothing references brings no record into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"program: the linker leaves it out. That happens with CocoaPods’ static libraries, a static"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"XCFramework, or a Bazel library with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alwayslink = False"},{"type":"text","text":". SwiftPM, and Bazel’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alwayslink = True"},{"type":"text","text":", link every object file. Link such a library whole ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-force_load"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Apple platforms, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--whole-archive"},{"type":"text","text":" on Linux) to have its events found."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference"},{"text":" holds the events of the images loaded when it is called: the program and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic libraries it links. A library opened later with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds its events from then on.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that loads or unloads while ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is read is either read whole or left out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that read. On Apple platforms one that dyld adds before the read starts is found; on Linux a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlclose"},{"text":" waits for the read, so the library is missed. The next read sees it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlclose"},{"text":" a library that declares events while the process runs. On Apple platforms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dyld keeps it mapped and its events are still found. On Linux the loader unmaps it while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift runtime keeps its types registered, and the process can crash later. Keep plug-ins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"open, or open them with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RTLD_NODELETE"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that declares events, linked into two images, lists each of its events twice, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores and plans refuse the duplicate. Link each such module into one image."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two events of one name in one linked image, the modules linked statically into one executable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or library, fail to build: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" gives each record a symbol named for the event’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which the compiler or the linker refuses to define twice. Separate images are never compared,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a name shared with a dynamic library, a library opened with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":", or a module linked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into two images is found only here, and a store or plan built from ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"},{"text":" refuses it. So is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one declared inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"private"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileprivate"},{"text":" type, whose symbol is local to its file.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"An event type found in the running program: one declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s own events, with its schema.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"DiscoveredEvent","modules":[{"name":"Events"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscoveredEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscoveredEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:6Events15DiscoveredEventV","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent.swift#L54","fileName":"DiscoveredEvent.swift"}},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Events/documentation/Events/EventSchema":{"title":"EventSchema","url":"\/documentation\/events\/eventschema","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventSchema"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventSchema"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The shape of an event type: its name, its schema version, its consent category and its stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties in declaration order, as a value tooling reads.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/ConsentCategory":{"title":"ConsentCategory","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsentCategory"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsentCategory"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","url":"\/documentation\/events\/consentcategory","abstract":[{"text":"The purpose an event is collected for, which the user consents to or refuses: analytics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"advertising and the like.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Event":{"url":"\/documentation\/events\/event","title":"Event","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Something that happened, recorded as a typed value.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/DiscoveredEvent/type":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"type","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": any (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Codable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Codablea"},{"text":").Type","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The event’s type.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/events\/discoveredevent\/type","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/type","kind":"symbol","title":"type","type":"topic"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/DiscoveredEvent/all":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every event type the program links, ordered by the UTF-8 bytes of their names, then by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version, then by the types’ fully qualified